                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1589d24-08b5-305b-aa7a-c36fe98def4a",
                        "entry_id": "e17ed71b-945d-32ff-913f-63a8d4d48156",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who diagnoses, especially a medical doctor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b097d19-f2fb-4ea8-8332-1567bff21067",
                                "sense_id": "b1589d24-08b5-305b-aa7a-c36fe98def4a",
                                "text": "Dr. Robert Leroy Hutton, a retired specialist in internal medicine and a well‐known diagnostician, died yesterday here."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a9767c7-5d4e-42ca-8e0d-163c5d3297fd",
                                "sense_id": "b1589d24-08b5-305b-aa7a-c36fe98def4a",
                                "text": "Dr Smith was many things — a mentor, a friend, a helpful colleague — but his highest calling may have been as a diagnostician, in which role he undoubtedly saved lives by breaking a logjam in many a challenging differential diagnosis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5193601-70b0-4239-8a9d-137bffa6a89a",
                                "sense_id": "b1589d24-08b5-305b-aa7a-c36fe98def4a",
                                "text": "\"More and more, the shrewdest thinkers and artists are precocious archeologists of ... ruins-in-the-making, indignant or stoical diagnosticians of defeat, enigmatic choreographers of the complex spiritual movements useful for individual survival in an era or permanent apocalypse.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0de673b-cd0a-439e-af09-955d616a2284",
                        "source_entry_id": "e17ed71b-945d-32ff-913f-63a8d4d48156",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1589d24-08b5-305b-aa7a-c36fe98def4a",
                        "source_sense_description": "a medical doctor specialized in diagnoses",
                        "target_lang_word": "interniste",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "interniste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dcacb4a5-259d-322a-b0f8-773d3be74b0e",
                                        "entry_id": "2a67b99f-e301-3317-a52c-2cc375d9f6ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Médecin spécialiste de médecine interne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce985aa6-e3d5-4498-aaae-4f305dffa3b5",
                                                "sense_id": "dcacb4a5-259d-322a-b0f8-773d3be74b0e",
                                                "text": "Du Dʳ House, tout le monde connaît le cynisme et l’humour grinçant. Mais on sait moins qu’il exerce une spécialité existant bel et bien, la médecine interne. Hugh Laurie est interniste (diagnostician en anglais), à ne pas confondre avec l’interne, étudiant en médecine de troisième cycle. En France, il existe plus de 2000 internistes, dont la plupart travaillent en milieu hospitalier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "386c7476-834f-40fb-b4c2-731910a64456",
                                                "sense_id": "dcacb4a5-259d-322a-b0f8-773d3be74b0e",
                                                "text": "Les internistes sont aussi les spécialistes de maladies rares ou dites « maladies orphelines » pouvant toucher plusieurs organes, telles que lupus, sclérodermie, Gougerot-Sjögren, polymyosite, vascularites, mastocytoses, histocytose, amylose, drépanocytose... Suivant les services, les internistes peuvent aussi prendre en charge des patients atteints de cancers, de maladies du sang ou génétiques."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
